 show like crazy ex-girlfriend not  only being made but  doing well and being praised for its  work feels like a step in the right  direction  of depicting mental health and mental  health professionals  in a more positive light but  it's also just one show  i deeply desperately hope that this is  the start of a trend and not a one-off  because  when we think about our loved ones or  ourselves seeking  mental health treatment our first  thoughts should not  include straight jackets padded rooms  and electroshock  that's not to say we couldn't all use a  jolt from time to time which brings us  to the sponsor's video  wait really we're really  going with that  [Music]  electroshock to caffeinated tea okay  zest tea offers a variety of products  from canned sparkling teas to more  traditional  bagged or loose leaf teas and even cbd  products with more caffeine than a cup  of coffee it's a way for tea drinkers to  get the energy  they need all products are available for  either a one-off purchase  or you can also subscribe for regular  deliveries and  be sure that you will never be short of  what you need  and if you use the link below and the  coupon code  nathaniel yes that is my name if you've  never watched the credits  if you use that you can get free  shipping on your first purchase  so that wraps up this one  depiction of mental health facilities  and professionals  what do you think about this what  examples would you offer of  positive depictions of mental health  workers and  if you've seen crazy ex-girlfriend  what's your favorite song from it  i'll always have a soft spot for the  sexy getting ready song but  i think i'd have to give the top spot to  you stupid [ __ ] that one's so epic  whatever your thoughts are drop them  down in the comments let's talk about it  and in addition today's sponsor this  channel is  as always supported by patreon there's  the thing  that keeps me fed and all the usual like  share subscribe  etc but i can't tell you what to do